  "title": "kerberos: Fix adding PA-SPAKE choice",
  "description": "The PA-SPAKE choice is not the value of PA-DATA, and should not be\nplaced in the private data struct for that. These are choices from\n0 to 4; PA-SPAKE itself is PA-DATA value 151.\n\nJust get the choice. Note that even though a ASN.1 CHOICE is always\nmapped to a FT_UINT field, the \"branch taken\" is a signed integer,\nso that -1 can be used for \"no branch found.\" (This is less than ideal.)\n\nAlso, update the URL and comment because SPAKE is no longer an I-D\nbut is published as RFC 9588: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/rfc9588/",
